1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:05,505
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:10,969 --> 00:00:14,014
<i>-You have to throw up!</i>
<i>-Guys, guys, I'm just joking.</i>

3
00:00:14,097 --> 00:00:16,099
<i>I didn't put poison in this.</i>

4
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:18,768
<i>I'd rather get married than mourn.</i>

5
00:00:18,852 --> 00:00:20,395
<i>Don't overshadow my moment.</i>

6
00:00:20,478 --> 00:00:23,898
<i>And I did tell you, Emilia. Don't try me.</i>

7
00:00:23,982 --> 00:00:25,358
-[grunts]
<i>-Emilia!</i>

8
00:00:25,442 --> 00:00:27,527
<i>Oh, Emilia. Help!</i>

9
00:00:27,610 --> 00:00:30,780
<i>-I love you! I love you!</i>
<i>-Reporting for duty, Mayor.</i>

10
00:00:30,864 --> 00:00:32,699
<i>-Madrigal.</i>
<i>-Just like old times, Mayor.</i>

11
00:00:32,782 --> 00:00:35,326
<i>The only difference is that</i>
<i>I work for Jaguar now.</i>

12
00:00:35,994 --> 00:00:36,870
[gunshots]

13
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,123
<i>What was that?! Secure Arnaldo, hurry!</i>

14
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:42,417
<i>Emilia? Emilia?</i>

15
00:00:43,334 --> 00:00:44,461
<i>Don't worry, Emilia.</i>

16
00:00:44,544 --> 00:00:47,464
<i>You'll regain your strength. Believe me.</i>

17
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:49,716
[Emilia] <i>Why don't you want to</i>
<i>show your face to me?</i>

18
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,384
[Raul] <i>Because your opinion of</i>
<i>me might change.</i>

19
00:00:51,468 --> 00:00:54,137
[Arnaldo] <i>If he thinks Jaguar</i>
<i>can protect him, he's wrong.</i>

20
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:57,057
<i>-Madrigal works for Jaguar?</i>
<i>-Yes.</i>

21
00:00:57,140 --> 00:00:59,225
<i>What's that? Why are you wounded?!</i>

22
00:00:59,309 --> 00:01:00,643
<i>Anna, this is nothing.</i>

23
00:01:00,727 --> 00:01:03,563
<i>What if you get caught next time?</i>
<i>Or worse, they kill you?</i>

24
00:01:03,646 --> 00:01:05,190
<i>I won't let them catch me alive!</i>

25
00:01:05,273 --> 00:01:06,524
<i>I'd rather shoot myself in the head, Anna!</i>

26
00:01:06,608 --> 00:01:08,443
<i>I'll do anything to stop them</i>
<i>from getting married.</i>

27
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:10,320
[Ivy] <i>The Jepoy that I knew</i>

28
00:01:10,403 --> 00:01:13,448
<i>would never join forces</i>
<i>with that monster Jaguar.</i>

29
00:01:13,531 --> 00:01:15,408
<i>Fine, Ivy. I've changed.</i>

30
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,743
<i>I let my emotions control my decisions.</i>

31
00:01:16,826 --> 00:01:18,912
<i>But I did everything for you.</i>

32
00:01:18,995 --> 00:01:20,371
<i>I let my feelings get the best of me</i>

33
00:01:20,455 --> 00:01:23,041
<i>because I love you, not just as a friend!</i>

34
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:24,584
<i>I love you, Ivy.</i>

35
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:27,545
[Emilia] <i>I must admit, I enjoy</i>
<i>the feeling of being bad.</i>

36
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,297
<i>I didn't know you were a great lover.</i>

37
00:01:29,380 --> 00:01:31,007
<i>That's why I've made my decision.</i>

38
00:01:31,090 --> 00:01:33,092
<i>We'll take my father down together.</i>

39
00:01:33,176 --> 00:01:35,261
<i>You'll make my dream come true.</i>

40
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:39,766
<i>You and I will be the king</i>
<i>and queen of this province.</i>

41
00:01:39,849 --> 00:01:43,603
<i>-Was I wrong to love Ivy?</i>
<i>-It's never wrong to love.</i>

42
00:01:43,686 --> 00:01:46,231
<i>It's just that sometimes</i>
<i>some things aren't meant to be.</i>

43
00:01:46,314 --> 00:01:48,399
<i>It's not like they can't understand.</i>

44
00:01:48,483 --> 00:01:51,277
<i>They're just scared something</i>
<i>bad might happen to you.</i>

45
00:01:51,361 --> 00:01:53,947
<i>Diego, I know how deeply</i>
<i>concerned you are.</i>

46
00:01:54,030 --> 00:01:56,533
<i>But this is a risk I have to take.</i>

47
00:01:58,743 --> 00:01:59,828
<i>Hon.</i>

48
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,996
<i>Grandpa and I decided that from</i>
<i>tonight until the wedding day,</i>

49
00:02:02,080 --> 00:02:03,456
<i>you'll just stay here.</i>
<i>You aren't going out.</i>

50
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,749
<i>It's like you've imprisoned me.</i>

51
00:02:04,833 --> 00:02:06,543
<i>That's exactly what it is.</i>

52
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:08,628
<i>It should be like this,</i>
<i>so no one can steal you from me.</i>

53
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:10,463
<i>This wedding must and will happen.</i>

54
00:02:26,646 --> 00:02:27,814
Ivy!

55
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:32,777
I'm so glad I can finally visit
the imprisoned bride.

56
00:02:33,486 --> 00:02:34,654
Are you sure?

57
00:02:34,737 --> 00:02:37,365
Yes, I am sure. I promise.

58
00:02:37,949 --> 00:02:40,785
The reason I came here is to apologize.

59
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:44,956
I'm sorry for what I did
during the bridal shower.

60
00:02:45,665 --> 00:02:48,376
I realized I shouldn't go against you.

61
00:02:49,127 --> 00:02:50,628
Really, Emilia?

62
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:52,714
Yes. I sincerely mean it.

63
00:02:53,965 --> 00:02:57,302
[sighs] I want the
wedding to push through,

64
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:00,388
so I can finally
welcome you to the family.

65
00:03:02,765 --> 00:03:03,725
Sometimes, you're mean,

66
00:03:03,808 --> 00:03:06,144
but you're sweet most of the time.

67
00:03:07,437 --> 00:03:08,271
Of course.

68
00:03:08,354 --> 00:03:10,356
And since you want to
welcome me to your family,

69
00:03:10,440 --> 00:03:15,695
can I call you Mom from now on?

70
00:03:20,283 --> 00:03:22,827
Yes! Sure. [chuckles]

71
00:03:23,995 --> 00:03:26,289
Daughter-in-law?

72
00:03:34,672 --> 00:03:35,798
[chuckles]

73
00:03:36,299 --> 00:03:37,258
[Emilia] Um…

74
00:03:37,342 --> 00:03:42,388
So, anyway, just relax here
in your little prison.

75
00:03:42,472 --> 00:03:44,432
But I'm sure you won't die or anything.

76
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:49,646
Bye.

77
00:03:50,146 --> 00:03:51,648
You too, <i>Mom</i>.

78
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:54,817
Relax and be careful
with what you eat and drink.

79
00:03:54,901 --> 00:03:56,986
What with the poison and all.

80
00:03:57,570 --> 00:03:58,613
But I'm sure you won't die.

81
00:03:58,696 --> 00:04:02,075
[tense music playing]

82
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:06,746
Not just yet.

83
00:04:07,413 --> 00:04:09,207
Your grave still needs to be dug.

84
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,960
Just you wait, <i>Mom</i>.

85
00:04:12,543 --> 00:04:13,920
It'll be worth it.

86
00:04:22,303 --> 00:04:28,726
I want the perimeter of the
wedding venue tightly secured.

87
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:36,067
If needed, let's place snipers
in strategic areas.

88
00:04:36,401 --> 00:04:38,403
Deploy your private army too.

89
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:41,155
I want a lot of men standing by.

90
00:04:41,239 --> 00:04:42,740
And place barbed wire to be safe.

91
00:04:42,824 --> 00:04:45,410
Understood, Mayor.
Understood, Congressman.

92
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:49,122
And while we're at it, bring fire trucks.

93
00:04:49,205 --> 00:04:50,790
Just in case we need to disperse people.

94
00:04:50,873 --> 00:04:52,292
Because our intel

95
00:04:52,375 --> 00:04:55,044
suggests people
will be protesting in the plaza.

96
00:04:55,128 --> 00:04:55,920
[Julio scoffs]

97
00:04:56,004 --> 00:04:58,381
The nerve of those people.

98
00:04:58,464 --> 00:05:02,927
Anyway, I don't want
your security people to be lax.

99
00:05:03,011 --> 00:05:04,762
I want you to punish the protesters

100
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:06,055
if they get in your way.

101
00:05:06,139 --> 00:05:07,807
Disperse them harshly.

102
00:05:07,890 --> 00:05:12,603
If anyone starts trouble, shoot them down,

103
00:05:12,687 --> 00:05:15,231
so they'll know that I mean business.

104
00:05:19,694 --> 00:05:22,071
Sit and have some rest.
We still have a long way.

105
00:05:22,155 --> 00:05:23,823
Food is on its way.

106
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:25,408
Okay? And water.

107
00:05:25,908 --> 00:05:27,785
-Use your time to rest.
-All right.

108
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:30,163
-We have a long day ahead.
-This guy's gonna like eating.

109
00:05:30,788 --> 00:05:32,915
[Marlon] Danny, don't let them
touch the floor.

110
00:05:32,999 --> 00:05:36,836
[Fernan] Look at it, it's dirty.
This is dirty.

111
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:38,129
What's the deal?

112
00:05:39,630 --> 00:05:41,591
Batch? What's wrong?

113
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,846
The wedding's tomorrow.

114
00:05:48,723 --> 00:05:50,016
Are you ready?

115
00:05:50,892 --> 00:05:52,643
I'm not thinking about myself anymore.

116
00:05:53,895 --> 00:05:56,647
Batch, we need to be alert.

117
00:05:59,067 --> 00:06:00,777
Something big will happen tomorrow.

118
00:06:02,361 --> 00:06:04,072
What do you mean? What's going to happen?

119
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:05,823
You'll know.

120
00:06:06,741 --> 00:06:08,326
We just have to be ready.

121
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,917
Come on, let's go back to the campaign.

122
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:17,251
You sure you're okay?

123
00:06:17,794 --> 00:06:18,836
All right.

124
00:06:19,712 --> 00:06:21,005
So, you guys doing okay?

125
00:06:21,089 --> 00:06:25,927
[tense music playing]

126
00:06:50,284 --> 00:06:51,702
<i>It's all right.</i>

127
00:06:51,786 --> 00:06:57,125
<i>You can imprison me in here,</i>
<i>but you can't stop my plans.</i>

128
00:06:59,252 --> 00:07:00,461
[phone ringing]

129
00:07:04,966 --> 00:07:05,800
Mom?

130
00:07:07,218 --> 00:07:08,219
Lily.

131
00:07:10,847 --> 00:07:12,640
Lily, I want to see you…

132
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:16,519
<i>I want to be with you before your wedding.</i>

133
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:18,771
<i>Please?</i>

134
00:07:19,230 --> 00:07:20,940
Can I see you today?

135
00:07:22,150 --> 00:07:24,902
Okay, Mom. I'll be there.

136
00:07:24,986 --> 00:07:26,320
Thank you, Lily.

137
00:07:35,663 --> 00:07:37,665
[music slowly fades]

138
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:47,884
Tomorrow, you're going to be
Mrs. Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

139
00:07:48,759 --> 00:07:49,802
Mm-hmm.

140
00:07:51,012 --> 00:07:53,389
And I can't wait, hon.

141
00:07:53,473 --> 00:07:54,599
Me neither.

142
00:07:55,516 --> 00:07:57,602
I really can't wait.

143
00:07:58,186 --> 00:07:59,854
Just one more--

144
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,314
Mmm.

145
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:03,774
-Come on!
-Arnaldo!

146
00:08:04,484 --> 00:08:05,276
Come on, Ivy.

147
00:08:05,359 --> 00:08:10,072
If I had my way, I would like to
spend the night here with you.

148
00:08:10,156 --> 00:08:11,491
Please, let me.

149
00:08:12,366 --> 00:08:15,244
Hon. I want that too.

150
00:08:15,328 --> 00:08:20,333
But I'm holding back because
I'm scared of the saying.

151
00:08:20,416 --> 00:08:23,503
The bride and groom can't be
together before they get married

152
00:08:23,586 --> 00:08:26,506
because the wedding
might not push through.

153
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:29,509
Do you want that?
We're going to have bad luck.

154
00:08:29,592 --> 00:08:30,968
The wedding won't happen.

155
00:08:31,636 --> 00:08:34,472
Of course, you don't. I know I don't.

156
00:08:37,475 --> 00:08:38,518
So?

157
00:08:39,894 --> 00:08:40,937
Okay.

158
00:08:42,021 --> 00:08:44,815
I'm just scared that when I wake up…

159
00:08:46,567 --> 00:08:47,777
you'll be gone.

160
00:08:48,611 --> 00:08:50,780
You've left and gone far away.

161
00:08:51,113 --> 00:08:52,657
No, hon.

162
00:08:53,241 --> 00:08:54,617
I'm not going anywhere.

163
00:08:55,201 --> 00:08:56,452
I'm not leaving you.

164
00:08:57,495 --> 00:09:00,206
Tomorrow, I'll be at our wedding.

165
00:09:02,542 --> 00:09:04,961
I'll be there in the church, hon.

166
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:07,797
I promise.

167
00:09:08,548 --> 00:09:09,840
I'll be there.

168
00:09:12,802 --> 00:09:13,970
Okay.

169
00:09:14,720 --> 00:09:16,222
I'll take your word for it.

170
00:09:19,934 --> 00:09:21,686
Hmm. Go on.

171
00:09:22,436 --> 00:09:26,065
It's getting really difficult
to control myself, Arnaldo.

172
00:09:27,233 --> 00:09:29,151
Tomorrow, I'm yours.

173
00:09:29,235 --> 00:09:32,280
[suspenseful music]

174
00:09:32,363 --> 00:09:34,323
-Tomorrow?
-Mm-hmm.

175
00:09:35,866 --> 00:09:37,034
Okay.

176
00:09:37,785 --> 00:09:38,995
Rest.

177
00:09:40,329 --> 00:09:45,418
Mrs. Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo.

178
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:47,378
I like the sound of that.

179
00:09:48,838 --> 00:09:50,756
-Good night, hon.
-Good night.

180
00:09:51,090 --> 00:09:52,842
Don't I get a goodnight kiss?

181
00:09:53,676 --> 00:09:54,760
Here.

182
00:09:55,761 --> 00:09:58,180
See? You're making this hard for me.

183
00:09:58,264 --> 00:09:59,724
It's just here.

184
00:10:01,267 --> 00:10:02,560
Okay, bye.

185
00:10:03,394 --> 00:10:04,604
-Hon, bye.
-See?

186
00:10:04,687 --> 00:10:07,231
I'm having a hard time when you do that.

187
00:10:07,565 --> 00:10:08,816
-One more day.
-I'll see you tomorrow.

188
00:10:08,899 --> 00:10:09,900
One more day.

189
00:10:09,984 --> 00:10:11,402
I'll see you tomorrow.

190
00:10:11,485 --> 00:10:14,780
One more day, one more day, one more day…

191
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:19,619
[ominous music playing]

192
00:10:19,702 --> 00:10:21,829
Be ready tomorrow, Arnaldo.

193
00:10:56,322 --> 00:11:01,494
[suspenseful music playing]

194
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:40,574
Oh, Lily. Why aren't you here yet?

195
00:11:48,332 --> 00:11:49,834
[heavy breathing]

196
00:11:53,003 --> 00:11:54,004
Mom.

197
00:11:55,047 --> 00:11:56,298
Lily, dear!

198
00:11:57,466 --> 00:12:01,345
[instrumental theme music playing]

199
00:12:04,723 --> 00:12:07,476
I thought I'd never get
to see you before your wedding.

200
00:12:09,311 --> 00:12:10,855
Lily, I'm scared.

201
00:12:19,238 --> 00:12:23,617
Lily, I can't imagine you
getting married to our enemy.

202
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:26,829
What if they keep you away from me?

203
00:12:28,205 --> 00:12:32,251
What if this is the last time
that I'll get to hold you?

204
00:12:35,963 --> 00:12:37,465
Mom, that's not going to happen.

205
00:12:39,592 --> 00:12:41,635
I already told you that the Ardientes

206
00:12:41,719 --> 00:12:43,095
will never keep us apart.

207
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:45,389
Never again.

208
00:12:48,017 --> 00:12:50,019
Mom, just have faith in me.

209
00:12:51,979 --> 00:12:53,397
Trust me, Mom.

210
00:13:04,992 --> 00:13:06,285
I'm sorry, Mom.

211
00:13:19,173 --> 00:13:22,301
[instrumental theme music
continues playing]

212
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:42,446
Miss Prianka…

213
00:13:46,492 --> 00:13:47,576
Thank you.

214
00:13:48,744 --> 00:13:51,413
Thank you so much for what you did.

215
00:13:53,415 --> 00:13:55,876
Thank you for everything you've taught me.

216
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:58,963
Ivy Aguas wouldn't exist…

217
00:14:02,007 --> 00:14:03,008
if it weren't for you.

218
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:08,806
I wouldn't be able to attain
justice if it weren't for you.

219
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:15,896
Thank you, Miss Prianka.

220
00:14:40,588 --> 00:14:41,714
Dad…

221
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:46,510
Dad, we were so happy then.

222
00:14:50,723 --> 00:14:52,850
Our family used to be happy…

223
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:58,147
until the Ardientes destroyed it.

224
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:04,945
Dad, do you remember my promise…

225
00:15:07,615 --> 00:15:08,991
to get justice?

226
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:12,411
It's within my reach, Dad.

227
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:14,788
And I promise you, Dad…

228
00:15:16,624 --> 00:15:21,462
that after I succeed,
Mom and I will be all right.

229
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:28,427
[somber music playing]

230
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:34,808
But my family will never be
complete without you here, Dad.

231
00:15:42,691 --> 00:15:44,234
This is for you, Dad.

232
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:49,782
This is for our family.

233
00:16:13,389 --> 00:16:16,058
I was the lucky one, Nanny.

234
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:20,562
I was so lucky you were there.

235
00:16:22,773 --> 00:16:28,404
Because you gave me all your love.

236
00:16:29,321 --> 00:16:32,992
You loved me with all your heart,

237
00:16:33,575 --> 00:16:35,828
that's why I'm so fortunate.

238
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,499
And that's why it still hurts.

239
00:16:42,042 --> 00:16:44,461
It hurts so much.

240
00:16:44,545 --> 00:16:48,424
And I hate myself
for dragging you into this mess.

241
00:16:49,883 --> 00:16:53,095
You were a victim
in my search for revenge!

242
00:16:55,305 --> 00:16:56,515
Nanny.

243
00:16:59,226 --> 00:17:02,146
Nanny, please forgive me.

244
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:06,525
I'm sorry for getting you involved

245
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:08,318
in my search for revenge!

246
00:17:14,658 --> 00:17:16,035
[sobbing]

247
00:17:17,202 --> 00:17:19,329
I promise you,

248
00:17:19,955 --> 00:17:24,084
I will make that bastard feel…

249
00:17:25,502 --> 00:17:28,172
just how tight a rope
around the neck can be.

250
00:17:30,215 --> 00:17:32,760
He'll pay with his life.

251
00:17:40,059 --> 00:17:42,227
I love you all so much.

252
00:17:42,311 --> 00:17:45,272
[dramatic music playing]

253
00:17:51,487 --> 00:17:53,906
[sobbing]

254
00:18:03,207 --> 00:18:06,001
[breathing deeply]

255
00:18:20,849 --> 00:18:24,228
[tense music playing]

256
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:28,941
<i>Everything will be over soon.</i>

257
00:18:33,237 --> 00:18:37,116
[tense music playing]

258
00:18:46,959 --> 00:18:49,211
[Dante] <i>Once we settle down</i>
<i>in Poblacion Ardiente,</i>

259
00:18:49,294 --> 00:18:50,796
<i>we'll have enough money to spare.</i>

260
00:18:50,879 --> 00:18:52,047
<i>And it won't be long</i>

261
00:18:52,131 --> 00:18:55,384
<i>until I build my own private law firm.</i>

262
00:18:55,467 --> 00:18:56,677
[young Lily] <i>Wow!</i>

263
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:01,181
[Dante] <i>This is going to be our new home!</i>

264
00:19:03,767 --> 00:19:05,602
[young Lily] <i>365 Days?</i>

265
00:19:05,686 --> 00:19:08,730
[Dante] <i>For an entire year full of love!</i>

266
00:19:09,106 --> 00:19:12,067
<i>We'll have the peaceful life</i>
<i>you've been dreaming of.</i>

267
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,450
[crying]

268
00:19:25,914 --> 00:19:27,124
<i>How dare you?!</i>

269
00:19:27,207 --> 00:19:28,917
<i>-You killed my husband!</i>
<i>-Mom, calm down.</i>

270
00:19:29,001 --> 00:19:31,128
<i>You murderers!</i>

271
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:32,921
-<i>What happened to you?</i>
-[shushes]

272
00:19:33,005 --> 00:19:34,047
[Tonio] <i>Hey!</i>

273
00:19:34,548 --> 00:19:37,176
<i>Lily… Run!</i>

274
00:19:40,721 --> 00:19:42,848
<i>Soon, this town will finally be free…</i>

275
00:19:43,599 --> 00:19:46,018
<i>from the Ardiente family's grip.</i>

276
00:19:49,688 --> 00:19:51,315
Hurry! Hurry! Here!

277
00:19:51,398 --> 00:19:52,566
Look over there.

278
00:19:52,649 --> 00:19:54,359
Here!

279
00:19:54,443 --> 00:19:57,988
-What--
-Why? Here!

280
00:19:58,071 --> 00:19:59,781
[indistinct chatter]

281
00:20:00,199 --> 00:20:01,909
-Step aside.
-Make way!

282
00:20:02,284 --> 00:20:03,869
[indistinct chatter]

283
00:20:07,748 --> 00:20:10,375
[suspenseful music playing]

284
00:20:26,642 --> 00:20:27,517
Hey, Grandpa.

285
00:20:29,561 --> 00:20:30,896
Arnaldo.

286
00:20:30,979 --> 00:20:31,897
[chuckles]

287
00:20:31,980 --> 00:20:33,065
Look at you!

288
00:20:34,775 --> 00:20:36,735
Dressed to the nines!

289
00:20:38,278 --> 00:20:40,989
What sartorial elegance.

290
00:20:41,073 --> 00:20:43,116
[chuckles] Thank you.

291
00:20:43,200 --> 00:20:44,785
I have a special gift for you.

292
00:20:46,703 --> 00:20:47,746
Wow!

293
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:52,042
Thank you, Grandpa!

294
00:20:52,834 --> 00:20:54,920
It seemed like the right gift.

295
00:20:55,545 --> 00:20:56,546
Very symbolic.

296
00:20:58,173 --> 00:21:01,385
My time is ending

297
00:21:01,468 --> 00:21:05,305
and yours is just about to start.

298
00:21:06,056 --> 00:21:07,057
[chuckling]

299
00:21:08,767 --> 00:21:11,687
I can't even believe
that you're getting married.

300
00:21:12,479 --> 00:21:13,981
Going back in time…

301
00:21:15,816 --> 00:21:20,654
I remember you as that bratty, little boy.

302
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:26,576
Now, you've grown up
to be a fine gentleman.

303
00:21:31,915 --> 00:21:35,335
You've come a long way, Arnaldo.

304
00:21:35,419 --> 00:21:36,878
[soft music playing]

305
00:21:36,962 --> 00:21:42,592
I'm so blessed
to have a grandson like you.

306
00:21:44,219 --> 00:21:48,307
I've been given a second chance
to feel like a father again.

307
00:21:49,349 --> 00:21:54,521
Because of your obedience
and your respect for me.

308
00:22:00,819 --> 00:22:02,779
You are the son…

309
00:22:05,032 --> 00:22:06,575
that I never had.

310
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:12,205
I'm so proud of you.

311
00:22:13,165 --> 00:22:14,833
I'm so proud of you, Arnaldo.

312
00:22:15,792 --> 00:22:16,835
Thank you, Grandpa.

313
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:19,046
I won't let you down.

314
00:22:19,629 --> 00:22:21,923
I know you won't. I know.

315
00:22:26,053 --> 00:22:27,137
[Emilia] Arnaldo.

316
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:29,306
[chuckles]

317
00:22:30,265 --> 00:22:31,725
Look at you!

318
00:22:31,808 --> 00:22:33,518
-You look so good!
-Thank you.

319
00:22:33,602 --> 00:22:34,978
-You look so great.
-Thank you.

320
00:22:35,896 --> 00:22:38,065
Looks like you're ready, but…

321
00:22:39,983 --> 00:22:42,027
I'm not ready to let you go.

322
00:22:45,822 --> 00:22:49,701
You understand why I'm like this, right?

323
00:22:50,535 --> 00:22:52,788
I mean, all mothers are like this.

324
00:22:52,871 --> 00:22:56,500
They want to protect their kids
from getting hurt.

325
00:22:58,335 --> 00:23:00,420
And, I'm sorry that I doubted you.

326
00:23:01,213 --> 00:23:02,798
I should've trusted you.

327
00:23:03,507 --> 00:23:06,093
I should've remembered
you were also an Ardiente,

328
00:23:06,176 --> 00:23:09,054
and Ardientes are strong, resilient,

329
00:23:09,137 --> 00:23:10,972
and, most of all, cunning.

330
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,767
[pensive music playing]

331
00:23:13,850 --> 00:23:15,852
I should've never doubted you.

332
00:23:16,311 --> 00:23:18,230
-It's okay, Mom.
-I love you, son.

333
00:23:18,313 --> 00:23:19,731
I love you too. I love you too.

334
00:23:19,815 --> 00:23:21,691
I'm sorry for everything.

335
00:23:21,775 --> 00:23:24,361
I'd already forgiven you. You and Dad.

336
00:23:24,444 --> 00:23:25,529
Thank you, son.

337
00:23:25,612 --> 00:23:29,116
And I figured we should let this wedding

338
00:23:29,199 --> 00:23:31,284
be a fresh start for all of us.

339
00:23:31,368 --> 00:23:32,953
And I'm looking forward to it.

340
00:23:33,870 --> 00:23:35,080
[Arnaldo] How does that sound?

341
00:23:35,163 --> 00:23:37,707
-Sounds fine to me.
-[Emilia and Raul chuckling]

342
00:23:37,791 --> 00:23:39,209
Sounds very fine.

343
00:23:39,292 --> 00:23:41,920
Let's give the groom a big hug.

344
00:23:44,256 --> 00:23:45,382
Viva Ardiente.

345
00:23:47,968 --> 00:23:49,803
[all] Viva Ardiente.

346
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:54,766
[dramatic music playing]

347
00:24:01,439 --> 00:24:02,983
Don't worry, Auntie.

348
00:24:04,484 --> 00:24:06,444
They'll definitely save Lily.

349
00:24:10,657 --> 00:24:13,952
[dramatic music swelling]

350
00:24:42,939 --> 00:24:45,483
Here's the package you've been
waiting for, Miss Aguas.

351
00:24:47,819 --> 00:24:50,864
And the Mayor and his family already left.

352
00:24:58,288 --> 00:25:02,250
[suspenseful music playing]

353
00:25:36,910 --> 00:25:40,121
We are now reporting live
at Poblacion Ardiente

354
00:25:40,205 --> 00:25:41,498
to witness the royal wedding

355
00:25:41,581 --> 00:25:44,334
of Mayor Arnaldo Ardiente-Torillo

356
00:25:44,417 --> 00:25:45,835
and Miss Ivy Aguas.

357
00:25:46,461 --> 00:25:50,298
Friends, citizens, please have a seat.

358
00:25:50,382 --> 00:25:51,633
The wedding's about to start.

359
00:25:52,050 --> 00:25:54,844
[no audible dialogue]

360
00:25:59,474 --> 00:26:01,851
<i>People are quickly</i>
<i>gathering outside the venue.</i>

361
00:26:02,978 --> 00:26:05,230
<i>The police and the military</i>
<i>are also in full force</i>

362
00:26:05,313 --> 00:26:06,815
<i>to ensure everyone's safety.</i>

363
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:09,567
<i>The cameras are in place</i>
<i>for the live coverage,</i>

364
00:26:09,651 --> 00:26:10,777
<i>which you can watch right here…</i>

365
00:26:10,860 --> 00:26:12,195
-Aisen! Aisen!
-<i>on the Ardiente TV Network…</i>

366
00:26:12,279 --> 00:26:14,698
-What?
-Look.

367
00:26:14,781 --> 00:26:16,324
<i>…at Poblacion Ardiente.</i>

368
00:26:16,408 --> 00:26:17,450
<i>So stay tuned!</i>

369
00:26:17,534 --> 00:26:19,327
<i>The royal wedding is about to start!</i>

370
00:26:20,328 --> 00:26:21,204
[kids] Yay!

371
00:26:21,288 --> 00:26:24,040
It's the Ardiente's royal wedding.

372
00:26:24,582 --> 00:26:27,335
-Oh, yeah!
-It's starting!

373
00:26:40,390 --> 00:26:43,268
[cheering]

374
00:26:49,607 --> 00:26:51,192
[indistinct chatter]

375
00:26:53,737 --> 00:26:58,366
[dreamy music playing]

376
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:10,295
<i>-Good afternoon, Madame.</i>
<i>-Good day.</i>

377
00:27:10,378 --> 00:27:11,796
[mouthing] Wow! It's beautiful!

378
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:14,883
[dreamy music continues]

379
00:27:16,009 --> 00:27:17,385
Shall we?

380
00:27:17,469 --> 00:27:19,179
Hello, friends.

381
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:30,857
[foreboding music playing]

382
00:27:39,491 --> 00:27:42,660
[foreboding music continues]

383
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,091
<i>I'm in position.</i>

384
00:28:08,603 --> 00:28:12,315
<i>I'll make sure no one</i>
<i>gets in your way, Ivy.</i>

385
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:15,860
<i>Not even the Ardientes themselves.</i>

386
00:28:18,696 --> 00:28:21,741
[tense music playing]

387
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:34,838
[foreboding music playing]

388
00:28:44,305 --> 00:28:47,016
Relax, Arnaldo.

389
00:28:47,809 --> 00:28:50,603
Nothing can stop your wedding.

390
00:28:52,897 --> 00:28:53,982
Ivy's late, Grandpa.

391
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,359
What if…

392
00:28:57,402 --> 00:28:58,820
What if she doesn't show up?

393
00:28:58,903 --> 00:28:59,988
[chuckles]

394
00:29:01,448 --> 00:29:03,742
Calm down, my son. Calm down.

395
00:29:04,868 --> 00:29:06,161
She'll be here.

396
00:29:11,958 --> 00:29:15,628
[tense music playing]

397
00:29:27,265 --> 00:29:28,308
Jepoy.

398
00:29:33,897 --> 00:29:35,231
What are you doing here?

399
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:37,484
You know why I'm here.
I'm gonna stop the wedding.

400
00:29:38,860 --> 00:29:40,779
And I'll stop whoever gets in my way.

401
00:29:41,154 --> 00:29:42,530
Even you, Diego.

402
00:29:43,907 --> 00:29:45,116
[Jepoy] I warned you.

403
00:29:45,784 --> 00:29:46,826
[gun cocks]

404
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:52,207
Jepoy, this isn't the right
time for you to interfere.

405
00:29:52,290 --> 00:29:54,542
What do we do? Nothing?

406
00:29:54,626 --> 00:29:56,711
-We let them get married?
-Ivy has plans.

407
00:30:00,048 --> 00:30:01,508
What do you know about Ivy's plans?

408
00:30:04,677 --> 00:30:05,762
Everything.

409
00:30:16,231 --> 00:30:20,360
[suspenseful music playing]

410
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:35,208
Excuse me, Papa.
I'll just make a phone call.

411
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,126
Don't take too long.

412
00:30:43,758 --> 00:30:48,513
[suspenseful music playing]

413
00:30:57,063 --> 00:31:00,066
[phone ringing]

414
00:31:01,359 --> 00:31:02,485
Are you in position?

415
00:31:02,569 --> 00:31:03,820
Yes, ma'am. I'm in position.

416
00:31:03,903 --> 00:31:05,864
Ready to fire once the bride arrives.

417
00:31:05,947 --> 00:31:06,781
Okay.

418
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:10,243
[grunting]

419
00:31:15,999 --> 00:31:21,546
Make sure that Ivy Aguas
doesn't enter the church alive.

420
00:31:21,629 --> 00:31:22,714
<i>Is that clear?</i>

421
00:31:22,797 --> 00:31:25,425
Your assassin's unconscious, Emilia.

422
00:31:25,717 --> 00:31:27,927
[tense music playing]

423
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:29,387
Diego?

424
00:31:34,976 --> 00:31:35,768
Diego…

425
00:31:36,519 --> 00:31:40,064
If you think I hired only one hitman,

426
00:31:40,148 --> 00:31:41,524
<i>then you're mistaken.</i>

427
00:31:41,983 --> 00:31:46,362
<i>If Ivy Aguas happens</i>
<i>to enter the church alive,</i>

428
00:31:46,446 --> 00:31:48,740
what makes you think
she'll get out alive too?

429
00:31:49,490 --> 00:31:50,408
What is it?

430
00:31:56,873 --> 00:31:58,207
You're going to have Ivy killed.

431
00:32:00,793 --> 00:32:02,879
Please, Raul, stay out of this.

432
00:32:02,962 --> 00:32:03,922
Stay out of this?

433
00:32:04,005 --> 00:32:06,341
If your father finds out
about this, he'll be furious.

434
00:32:06,424 --> 00:32:08,384
He wants this wedding to happen.

435
00:32:08,468 --> 00:32:11,846
No! Ivy Aguas has to die.

436
00:32:12,263 --> 00:32:14,098
Raul, she's going to replace me
in this family.

437
00:32:14,182 --> 00:32:15,308
Do you understand?

438
00:32:15,391 --> 00:32:17,310
If you destroy Arnaldo's life…

439
00:32:18,102 --> 00:32:21,898
He'll get over this heartache,
just like everybody does.

440
00:32:22,398 --> 00:32:24,734
And who's going to help him
if not his own mother?

441
00:32:25,568 --> 00:32:26,611
Remember, Raul…

442
00:32:27,028 --> 00:32:30,531
I got over the most painful
heartache in my life.

443
00:32:30,615 --> 00:32:32,742
And that's by getting over you.

444
00:32:32,825 --> 00:32:35,578
Is that it? You're over me? Are you sure?

445
00:32:37,121 --> 00:32:39,415
Enough, Raul. I don't have time for this.

446
00:32:39,499 --> 00:32:42,585
I have a bride to kill,
so if you'll excuse me.

447
00:32:45,880 --> 00:32:47,632
-There are other hitmen?
-Yeah.

448
00:32:47,715 --> 00:32:49,592
-How many?
-I don't know.

449
00:32:52,720 --> 00:32:53,471
Jepoy.

450
00:32:53,554 --> 00:32:56,015
Go inside, I'll handle this.
Go on. I'll follow.

451
00:32:56,099 --> 00:32:57,058
Okay.

452
00:33:02,814 --> 00:33:06,359
[woman] Ladies and gentlemen,
the bride is arriving.

453
00:33:06,442 --> 00:33:09,404
So, may I please ask everyone
to please go inside first,

454
00:33:09,487 --> 00:33:11,364
so we can start the ceremony?

455
00:33:12,865 --> 00:33:14,742
Let's go inside first, ma'am.

456
00:33:14,826 --> 00:33:17,078
Let's go inside, ma'am, okay?

457
00:33:17,161 --> 00:33:20,498
[cheers]

458
00:33:21,541 --> 00:33:23,459
Ivy! Ivy!

459
00:33:25,753 --> 00:33:29,298
[woman] Thank you. Let's get
inside, so we can begin.

460
00:33:29,966 --> 00:33:32,010
I need you to get inside.
Everyone, please…

461
00:33:32,093 --> 00:33:33,386
[indistinct chatter]

462
00:33:33,469 --> 00:33:35,888
Your wife-to-be is here, okay?

463
00:33:42,854 --> 00:33:44,272
Okay. Best man?

464
00:33:45,023 --> 00:33:46,024
Please stay here.

465
00:33:49,819 --> 00:33:50,778
-Oh, yes.
-Fall in line.

466
00:33:50,862 --> 00:33:51,904
-Okay.
-Thank you.

467
00:33:51,988 --> 00:33:53,239
-Okay, thank you.
-Miss Claire.

468
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:03,958
[dramatic music playing]

469
00:34:16,220 --> 00:34:21,017
[orchestra playing]

470
00:35:23,788 --> 00:35:29,293
[orchestra playing]

471
00:36:25,725 --> 00:36:30,354
[orchestra playing]

472
00:37:13,064 --> 00:37:14,941
[music slowly fades]

473
00:37:17,151 --> 00:37:22,907
[suspenseful music playing]

474
00:37:48,933 --> 00:37:53,020
[suspenseful music continues]

475
00:38:11,038 --> 00:38:16,252
[eerie music playing]

476
00:38:46,532 --> 00:38:52,371
[tense music playing]

477
00:39:03,674 --> 00:39:08,679
[tense music continues playing]

478
00:39:23,319 --> 00:39:24,945
<i>Yes, I'm wearing black.</i>

479
00:39:26,405 --> 00:39:30,493
<i>Because this is the only color</i>
<i>that suits this occasion.</i>

480
00:39:48,886 --> 00:39:55,810
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

481
00:40:48,821 --> 00:40:55,703
["Wildflower" instrumental continues]

482
00:41:41,707 --> 00:41:48,672
["Wildflower" instrumental continues]

483
00:41:58,807 --> 00:42:03,812
["Wildflower" instrumental continues]

484
00:42:29,338 --> 00:42:30,798
Did I surprise you?

485
00:42:33,509 --> 00:42:35,344
You were never one for tradition.

486
00:42:41,141 --> 00:42:42,142
Shall we?

487
00:42:57,992 --> 00:43:02,037
Papa, look how Ivy Aguas
is disrespecting us.

488
00:43:02,121 --> 00:43:05,249
I can't let her do this to the family.

489
00:43:07,376 --> 00:43:09,837
I don't give a hoot

490
00:43:09,920 --> 00:43:15,009
if she came here in black, pink, red,

491
00:43:15,092 --> 00:43:20,598
or wearing nothing
but that necklace on her neck.

492
00:43:21,807 --> 00:43:23,934
What matters to me is that she came

493
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:25,769
and that she will marry Arnaldo.

494
00:43:25,853 --> 00:43:30,024
And, in a little while,
she will be an Ardiente.

495
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:34,987
Now, if she's got something bad planned,

496
00:43:36,405 --> 00:43:40,951
she will suffer like
everyone else who does us wrong.

497
00:43:41,035 --> 00:43:43,871
[tense music playing]

498
00:43:47,499 --> 00:43:50,002
Come to think of it,
that black gown suits her, Papa.

499
00:43:51,962 --> 00:43:53,922
You're right, Raul. It does suit her.

500
00:43:54,006 --> 00:43:56,050
It's perfect for what
will happen to her later.

501
00:44:15,402 --> 00:44:19,657
[priest] <i>If anyone knows of any reason why</i>
<i>Ivy and Arnaldo should not be married,</i>

502
00:44:19,740 --> 00:44:23,118
<i>speak now or forever hold your peace.</i>

503
00:44:24,203 --> 00:44:25,162
[Jepoy] <i>What's that?</i>

504
00:44:25,245 --> 00:44:26,872
<i>-You're one of Emilia's hitmen.</i>
<i>-No--</i>

505
00:44:26,955 --> 00:44:29,750
[grunting]

506
00:44:31,835 --> 00:44:33,128
[priest] <i>Do you, Arnaldo,</i>

507
00:44:33,212 --> 00:44:36,173
<i>take Ivy to be your lawfully wedded wife?</i>

508
